cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The Hodge–Fermat Campaign: verifying the Integral Hodge
  Conjecture for high-dimensional Fermat varieties, and the
  prime-power reduction frontier
message: >-
  If you use these engines, results, or writing, please cite
  them using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Amichis Luengo
    given-names: Rafael
    city: Madrid
    country: ES
    email: tretoef@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/tretoef-estrella/prime-power-frontier'
abstract: >-
  A computational campaign verifying the Integral Hodge
  Conjecture for high-dimensional Fermat varieties on a single
  8 GB laptop, via the Degtyarev–Shimada combinatorial
  primitivity criterion. Eight cells were given complete
  PRIMITIVE verdicts, including (6,6) — the first
  composite-degree cell verified — and the work identified the
  prime-power reduction frontier, the exact boundary at which
  the Jordan-mould reduction silently fails.
keywords:
  - Hodge conjecture
  - Fermat varieties
  - algebraic geometry
  - computational mathematics
  - exact linear algebra
  - finite fields
